# q38-27b-iq3r-l.recipe -- IQ3R-L: Qwen3.8-27B on IQ8R's rotated int8 grid at ~3.80 bits a weight.
# Every trunk linear rotated by fwht128 and fitted by GPTQ against the calib Hessians with a bf16
# scale per (row, 128): 4096 4-wide codewords (3 bits, dyn=1) in layers 0-23; the 16-level scalar
# codebook (dyn=1, cd=8, damp=0.05) in layers 24-63 (docs/IQR.md, "Where the bits go"). Embedding:
# the 16-level scalar codebook by rtn; head: the 16-level scalar codebook by GPTQ against the head's
# input Hessian. libr4d decodes every code where it is read (gemm_iqr); served by qwen35_w8a8 at
# i8a8h with rotated int8 activations.
#
#   CALIB=<calib Hessians, RADGRAM2> rad-convert <Qwen3.8-27B bf16> --recipe data/recipes/q38-27b-iq3r-l.recipe \
#       --set quantization_config.quant_method=w8a8 --set quantization_config.fmt=fwht128 -o OUT.rad
#
# run from the repository root (the vq= paths are relative to it).
# The competition's private tiers 1+2: 3.798 bpw, mean KL 0.01887, top-1 94.78% (UD-Q3_K_XL: 3.803, 0.02403).

blk.0.ssm_inz.weight gptq vq=data/codebooks/iqr-vq3-4x4096.txt group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 dyn=1 calib=$CALIB
blk.0.ssm_out.weight gptq vq=data/codebooks/iqr-vq3-4x4096.txt group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 dyn=1 calib=$CALIB
blk.0.ffn_gate_up.weight gptq vq=data/codebooks/iqr-vq3-4x4096.txt group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 dyn=1 calib=$CALIB
blk.0.ffn_down.weight gptq vq=data/codebooks/iqr-vq3-4x4096.txt group=128 scale=bf16 transform=fwht128 dyn=1 calib=$CALIB
